    "solution": "Place the blue mouth in the marked western floor, collect the lantern, and carry it into the link. After arriving on the eastern belt, walk left through the grill while still carrying the weight. Closing the blue link restores the orange opening as solid wall. Return right, stop steering and set the lantern down onto the belt. It now parks against the former mouth on the pressure plate instead of returning to the start. Jump over that wall and continue through the held-open door. The two separated door leaves need a sustained weight: the belt\u2019s brief passing contact cannot hold the whole exit passage open.",
    "nearestExisting": "Open the Other End (F20, banked in Base) repositions a portal to change which side of a stone can be reached; B20 preserves a closed door as a ladder. This room closes its useful transport link to turn the receiving wall into a conveyor stop, with the same weight then maintaining the exit.",
    "novelty": "The transport opening is initially the reason the delivery will not stay delivered. Destroying the link restores the piece of architecture that the belt needs as its stop.",
